    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d895-a1">

                <pb facs="0905" n="647" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg647"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Austro-Hungarian Charge at Washington</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Zwiedinek</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Austro-Hungarian Minister of Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Burian</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 19, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>272. I have just been informed by Secretary of State that my personal suggestion
                    “that a possible solution of the <hi rendition="#italic">Ancona</hi> case might
                    be found if Austro-Hungarian Government would agree that such attacks should not
                    be repeated and if consideration of the law and fact relating to the sinking of
                    the Ancona were then continued,” [is] entirely unacceptable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Zwiedinek</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
